{"summary":"The black sparrowhawk (Astur melanoleucus), sometimes known as the black goshawk or great sparrowhawk, is a bird of prey belonging to the family Accipitridae. It was formerly placed in the genus Accipiter. It occurs mainly in forest and non-desert areas south of the Sahara, particularly where there are large trees suitable for nesting; favored habitat includes suburban and human-altered landscapes. It preys predominantly on birds of moderate size, such as pigeons and doves, in suburban areas.","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_sparrowhawk","cells":[[-18.3,21.4,1],[-19.6,15.8,1],[-19.0,32.7,2],[-15.6,28.5,1],[-15.6,35.5,1],[-16.3,35.5,2],[-15.6,34.8,2],[-16.3,34.8,1],[-20.3,28.5,1],[-17.6,31.3,2],[-34.6,20.7,1],[-33.4,22.1,1],[-32.2,18.6,1],[-34.0,19.3,2],[-22.9,14.4,1],[-34.6,18.6,1],[-32.2,19.3,1],[-31.7,18.6,1],[-34.6,20.0,2],[-33.4,20.0,2],[-34.0,20.0,2],[-30.4,22.1,1],[-33.4,18.6,2],[-33.4,21.4,2],[-34.6,19.3,2],[-34.0,22.1,3],[-34.0,20.7,2],[-34.0,18.6,3],[-26.7,30.6,1],[-26.7,32.0,1],[-29.2,27.8,1],[-30.4,25.0,1],[-33.4,22.9,1],[-28.0,31.3,1],[-32.8,28.5,1],[-26.1,26.4,1],[-33.4,23.6,1],[-32.8,27.8,1],[-27.4,28.5,1],[-26.7,29.2,1],[-26.1,31.3,1],[-26.1,32.0,1],[-32.2,27.1,1],[-24.8,31.3,1],[-24.8,28.5,1],[-28.0,32.0,1],[-30.4,27.1,1],[-24.2,30.6,1],[-28.0,30.6,1],[-27.4,32.7,1],[-33.4,25.0,1],[-33.4,25.7,2],[-25.5,30.6,1],[-25.5,27.8,2],[-34.0,23.6,1],[-26.7,31.3,1],[-32.2,24.3,1],[-26.7,27.8,2],[-29.8,29.2,1],[-24.2,28.5,1],[-29.8,29.9,1],[-28.6,32.7,2],[-28.6,29.2,1],[-28.6,28.5,1],[-28.0,32.7,1],[-32.8,27.1,1],[-22.9,29.2,1],[-25.5,29.2,1],[-26.7,26.4,1],[-34.0,25.0,1],[-25.5,27.1,2],[-24.8,27.1,1],[-25.5,26.4,1],[-29.2,31.3,2],[-29.2,29.9,1],[-27.4,29.9,1],[-29.2,29.2,1],[-26.1,29.9,1],[-25.5,29.9,1],[-29.2,26.4,1],[-26.7,29.9,1],[-26.7,32.7,1],[-26.7,28.5,1],[-22.9,31.3,1],[-25.5,31.3,2],[-31.1,29.9,1],[-24.2,29.9,1],[-29.2,30.6,2],[-31.1,30.6,1],[-30.4,22.1,1],[-27.4,31.3,1],[-33.4,26.4,1],[-29.2,32.0,2],[-27.4,32.0,1],[-26.1,27.1,2